### Tool-Specific Labeling (INVARIANT)
Every LEAF node in the tool_execution zone MUST have either a `tool_invocation` action with a `tool_id` matching a tool name from the Tool Inventory above, or an `integration_interaction` action with an `integration_id` matching an integration name from the External Integrations list. Use canonical names verbatim — never invent names. The human-readable `label` is display prose only; it does not determine tool or integration identity.

### Tool Execution Zone Scope (INVARIANT)
A node belongs in the tool_execution zone if and only if it represents either a canonical `tool_invocation` resolving a tool name from the Tool Inventory above, or a direct canonical `integration_interaction` resolving an integration name from the External Integrations list. If you cannot name a concrete tool or integration by its canonical name, the node does NOT belong in tool_execution. Generic action phrases like "Execute unauthorized X delivery" are not valid tool_execution nodes. If the attack outcome is the LLM generating text output rather than calling a tool or interacting with an integration, that step belongs in the reasoning zone, not tool_execution.
